    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. Start with two ordinary zero qubits. Apply Hadamard to the first, then controlled-NOT. Two gates turn a product state into a maximally entangled Bell pair.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Build a Bell pair with exactly H then CNOT.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — CIRCUITS",
            "segment": "Two Gates Tie the Knot",
            "greeting": "G'day, Liam",
            "runningText": "following product state into entanglement…",
            "output": [
              "H creates local superposition on the control.",
              "CNOT converts it into joint correlation."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 9,
      "narration_text": "The input is zero-zero. Each qubit has its own pure state, and the joint state factors into control times target.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "split"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "Hadamard sends the control from zero to plus: zero plus one over root two. The target stays zero.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "After H, the joint state is zero-zero plus one-zero over root two. It is a superposition, but still separable: plus tensor zero.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Now controlled-NOT flips the target only on the branch where the control is one. Zero-zero stays zero-zero; one-zero becomes one-one.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "The output is phi plus: zero-zero plus one-one over root two. No product of one-qubit states can reproduce it.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Measure both in the computational basis and the outcomes match perfectly: zero-zero or one-one, each with probability one half.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Yet each qubit alone is maximally mixed. Its reduced Bloch vector sits at the center. That is not wave-function collapse; it is the local description of an entangled pure state.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "The information did not vanish. It moved into correlations: the joint state is perfectly known even though neither subsystem has its own pure state.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "Order matters. CNOT on zero-zero does nothing; applying H afterward creates a product superposition, not this Bell pair.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. After Hadamard but before CNOT, are the qubits entangled? Pause before the answer: no. The state is plus tensor zero. CNOT is the gate that converts branch-dependent action into entanglement.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Your turn: is H alone enough to entangle the pair?",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — CHECK",
            "segment": "Superposition Versus Entanglement",
            "greeting": "Over to you, Liam",
            "runningText": "waiting for the factorization test…",
            "output": [
              "After H: |+> tensor |0>, still separable.",
              "After CNOT: |Phi+>, entangled."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B11.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:28:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "estimated_duration_s": 8,
      "narration_text": "Two gates tie the quantum knot: H creates branches, and CNOT ties the target to which branch occurred.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "fade"
      },
